class:: FFTMKL2
summary:: Modified Kullback-Leibler spectral deviation
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/FFTFlux2

description::
Sum of log(1 + currentMagnitude / (previousMagnitude + epsilon)). This is the modified spectral divergence used by OnsetsDS, independently implemented. Stationary nonzero bins contribute approximately log(2), so this is an evidence function with a baseline, not a trigger or a zero-at-stationarity distance. No adaptive whitening is applied.

DC and Nyquist are excluded from the evidence; normalization includes their two positions in the bin count. Raw FFT magnitudes are used without window or FFT-size compensation. The first two valid frames output zero while the phase predictor warms up. Results hold between FFT frames. Persistent storage is allocated at construction; the FFT buffer is read without modifying its representation. Like vanilla Onsets, this exposes spectral onset evidence, but it has no peak picking. Use Onsets2 for triggers.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
An FFT chain with the declared size.
argument:: epsilon
Positive denominator floor, default 1e-6.
argument:: normalize
Positive divides by the one-sided bin count.
argument:: fftSize
Literal matching FFT size, a power of two from 256 through 8192.
returns::
One nonnegative control-rate evidence value.

examples::
The measured spectral change opens a filtered noise accompaniment over the source.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source);
        var value = FFTMKL2.kr(chain);
        var texture = BPF.ar(PinkNoise.ar(0.15), 1800, 0.5) * (value * 1).clip(0, 1).lag(0.03);
        (source * 0.16 + texture) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.25) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

